/> Awareness 3, Dodge 2,<br /> Crafts 3, Melee 3, Stealth 3<br /> Academics 2, Cosmology 2, Investigation 2, Occult 3<br /> <br /> Auspex 2, Thaumaturgy 2 (Creatio Ignis) <br /> Rituals: Levels: 1, 2<br /> <br /> Willpower 3<br /> Conviction 4, Self Control 3, Courage 3<br /> Domain 1, Generation 5, Herd1<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T08:54:25-07:00","id":1083994,"title":"","content":"Tactics are going to be a bigger mess. They're looking nasty on either side but a lot has to be determined first and I still haven't gotten around to reading all about the gargoyles. Also, I have to figure out what sorts of things the Gangrel and Tzimisce will send.<br /> <br /> So far, my idea is that the 3 nearby houses will be assembling a combined war party of some sort in one of the Order Chanties near Transylvania and then marching to somewhere not too far from the known Tremere HQ and attempting to conquer it, hoping first to keep it intact, and then destroying the place utterly if that fails.<br /> <br /> The Tremere on the other hand will have wiped out or driven off other Order mages in Transylvania and will be doing their best to indirectly harass this war party until it reaches the supposed Tremere HQ, which they have likely turned into some sort of trap. If the death trap, harassment, and the strain of travel through Transylvania has taken its toll on the War party, they will mount a major offensive in an attempt to wipe out these guys.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, other Tremere groups will be attempting to blood bind mages left in the nearby Order strongholds just outside of Transylvania.<br /> <br /> At this point, the Gangrel who, assisted by the Nosferatu, are looking for some opportunity to deal a major blow to the Tremere, will notice the Mage war band and try and figure out how to take advantage of it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T10:44:22-07:00","id":1084056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the meantime, other Tremere groups will be attempting to blood bind mages left in the nearby Order strongholds just outside of Transylvania.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how do you pruposse to do this with the Tremere House having been declared traitor?. Surely all Tremere are going to be expelled from all &quot;Order strongholds&quot; before any war band get's formed or delivered. Mercere &quot;red caps&quot; are going to be delivering the memo to everyone, and they are very efficient. A judgement of one major House it's not a small thing that the rest of the Order can ignore, after all. Worse, since the Tremere were inteligent enough to have &quot; wiped out or driven off other Order mages&quot;, then these nearby Chantries have refugees that will not trust in any Tremere. Most likely the Tremere in these chantries are dead or under scrutiny, and the chantries have already activated the Aegis and any other ward they may have!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So far, my idea is that the 3 nearby houses will be assembling a combined war party of some sort in one of the Order Chanties near Transylvania and then marching to somewhere not too far from the known Tremere HQ and attempting to conquer it, hoping first to keep it intact, and then destroying the place utterly if that fails. </div> </div> </div>And how are the Hermetics going to implement this <i>clever plan</i>? .<br /> <br /> It seems to me that, strategy wise, you're returning to the old &quot;let's group the mages and charge!&quot;, &quot;surely a major House known for it's intriges won't have discovered that they were under trial for three whole days and we can surprise them, even when they're at the other side of Europe!&quot;. Leaving actual strategy for the Tremere <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's a HOUSE they're attacking, not a mere Chantry, and a Major House...one would think that taking their time to assure that nearby Order strongholds are well defended and gathering intelligence before attacking to seek weaknesses and strenghts on the enemy force would beat a Leeroy Jenkins approach. Look, I'm no strategist, I can barely win a campaign of Age of Empires with reloads, but even I know that's a bad idea, especially for a splat known for their dependence on preparation and their lack of instant power if surprised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T11:19:25-07:00","id":1084073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084056#post1084056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And how do you pruposse to do this with the Tremere House having been declared traitor?. Surely all Tremere are going to be expelled from all &quot;Order strongholds&quot; before any war band get's formed or delivered. Mercere &quot;red caps&quot; are going to be delivering the memo to everyone, and they are very efficient. A judgement of one major House it's not a small thing that the rest of the Order can ignore, after all. Worse, since the Tremere were inteligent enough to have &quot; wiped out or driven off other Order mages&quot;, then these nearby Chantries have refugees that will not trust in any Tremere. Most likely the Tremere in these chantries are dead or under scrutiny, and the chantries have already activated the Aegis and any other ward they may have!</div> </div> </div> </div>Working on covert plans and strategies for that, mostly involving stealth and tainting local beverages... and no, they will not go door to door giving drinks. Also, note the word &quot;attempting&quot;. It'll be a spy game with the Vampires doing their best to evade scrutiny of any sort. They could still fail miserably. (Edit: Incidentally, I never assumed this would be done as an inside job by Tremere Order mages among the Order Chantries. I'm assuming at this point that the Tremere have been expelled and any remaining loyal Tremere agents among the order are dead, unable to act due to the order announcements, or being counteracted by Tremere defectors. Any spying and sabotage on either side must now start anew with fresh agents who have to find their way behind enemy lines.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084056#post1084056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how are the Hermetics going to implement this <i>clever plan</i>? .<br /> <br /> It seems to me that, strategy wise, you're returning to the old &quot;let's group the mages and charge!&quot;, &quot;surely a major House known for it's intriges won't have discovered that they were under trial for three whole days and we can surprise them, even when they're at the other side of Europe!&quot;. Leaving actual strategy for the Tremere <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I'm trying at the moment to figure out a way for the mages to do this camped out a fairly safe distance from the fortress with their most powerful members casting ritual after ritual to maybe summon something to storm the gates of the enemy, while the rest of the party builds them a fortress and defends it. They most definitely won't walk into the place. My biggest hurdle is doing this in a way that won't simply level the Tremere stronghold... which they will do with powerful magic from a distance if they find it too inconvenient to win the battle otherwise. Also, note that the war party will be very well prepared for attack as well as probably invisible. Note that they don't have the same info gathering capabilities as some of the other mage groups of the time nor of the modern version of the Order. For one thing, their use of spirits wasn't quite what it is today. However, they are in no way going blind, and an actual surprise attack is a near impossibility. A Hermetic lookout will almost always know of impending attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084056#post1084056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a HOUSE they're attacking, not a mere Chantry, and a Major House...one would think that taking their time to assure that nearby Order strongholds are well defended and gathering intelligence before attacking to seek weaknesses and strenghts on the enemy force would beat a Leeroy Jenkins approach. Look, I'm no strategist, I can barely win a campaign of Age of Empires with reloads, but even I know that's a bad idea, especially for a splat known for their dependence on preparation and their lack of instant power if surprised.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they are not going to leave their strongholds undefended, but any mage that leaves a stronghold leaves it less defended. I'm actually going to have to figure out what specific stuff they'd leave behind as defenses.<br /> <br /> If you have specific suggestions on how this should go, I'd like them.<br /> <br /> <br /> To put you a bit at ease, I am trying to come up with the most exploitative ways to use each side's supernatural capabilities and other resources. For the mages, this currently includes long range catastrophy level effects, sunlight, attacking at day, and possibly dismantling the Tremere stronghold using something like telekinesis or flushing it with a horde of supernaturally enhanced mutated abominations. For the Tremere, it involves the use of the blood bond (which is one of the few things the mages will have little info on at this point), potions, artificially created vampires (gargoyles and their kin) and things like dominating entire populations including little children to try and kill the mages. It's just taking a while and I can't finalize any of it until I figure out what sort of war parties and units each side would build.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-26-2017, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T11:24:09-07:00","id":1084076,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Tremere just wanted to survive more than the Hermetics wanted to kill them. Tell a Hermetic that vampires are an abomination, and maybe he'll believe you, but is he going to want to risk his life over it? Wouldn't it be far more exciting to him to stay home and read that old tome, or mix these potions? Meanwhile the Tremere are devoting their every waking hour to not dying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T12:05:14-07:00","id":1084093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084076#post1084076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the Tremere just wanted to survive more than the Hermetics wanted to kill them. Tell a Hermetic that vampires are an abomination, and maybe he'll believe you, but is he going to want to risk his life over it? Wouldn't it be far more exciting to him to stay home and read that old tome, or mix these potions? Meanwhile the Tremere are devoting their every waking hour to not dying.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> essentially this is what happened. that and the hermetics having more pressing enemies(particularly the inquisition) .and there is this whole magic &quot;dying &quot;thing going on.<br /> also i'm not sure if anyone mentioned this but the tremere are entrenched.<br /> <br /> for instance there are very very few tremere in iberia and maybe none on scandinavia. hell almost half the clan is supposed to be in the carpathians and the nearby areas like lithuania,<br /> a very dangerous area by the way.<br /> <br /> meanwhile the order of hermes far superior strength is spread out throught europe and more.<br /> <br /> granted the tremere have a lot of vampiric enemies but the order as a whole is not aware of it. or at least making an alliance with other vampires is ..difficult at best for various reasons<br /> <br /> <br /> also i'd argue that by becoming a clan in 1133 the tremere become part of the &quot;shadowy&quot; vampiric consensus. in other words one could say that attemptin to destroy the tremere clan as a whole is a vulgar act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T21:38:39-07:00","id":1084323,"title":"","content":"The Gargoyles<br /> <br /> Fledgeling Gargoyle<br /> Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3,<br /> Charisma 1, Manipulation 4, Appearance 1<br /> Perception 3, Intelligence 2, Wits 3<br /> <br /> Alertness 2, Athletics 2, Awareness 1, Brawl 3, Dodge 3, Intimidation 2<br /> Animal Ken 3, Stealth 3, Survival 3<br /> Investigation 3, Occult 2<br /> <br /> Flight 2, Fortitude 1, Potence 1<br /> <br /> Willpower 4<br /> Conviction 2, Self Control 4, Courage 4<br /> Generation 3, Herd 1, Resources 1<br /> <br /> <br /> Neonate Gargoyle<br /> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 4,<br /> Charisma 1, Manipulation 5, Appearance 1<br /> Perception 4, Intelligence 2, Wits 5<br /> <br /> Alertness 3, Athletics 3, Awareness 1, Brawl 4, Dodge 4, Intimidation 2<br /> Animal Ken 4, Stealth 5, Survival 4<br /> Investigation 4, Occult 3, Politics 2<br /> <br /> Flight 3, Fortitude 2, Potence 2<br /> <br /> Willpower 5<br /> Conviction 3, Self Control 4, Courage 5<br /> Generation 3, Herd 1, Resources 2<br /> <br /> <br /> Older Gargoyle<br /> Strength 5, Dexterity 4, Stamina 5,<br /> Charisma 3, Manipulation 5, Appearance 1<br /> Perception 5, Intelligence 3, Wits 5<br /> <br /> Alertness 4, Athletics 4, Awareness 1, Brawl 4, Dodge 5, Intimidation 3<br /> Animal Ken 5, Stealth 5, Survival 5, Archery 2<br /> Investigation 5, Occult 4, Politics 4<br /> <br /> Flight 3, Fortitude 4, Potence 4<br /> <br /> Willpower 6<br /> Conviction 4, Self Control 5, Courage 5<br /> Generation 3, Herd 1, Resources 3<br /> <br /> 5880 Gargoyles.<br /> Round it to 103 groups of 1 Older gargoyle, 7 Neonates, &amp; 49 Fledgelings<br /> 103 + 721 + 5047 each (a remainder of 9)<br /> <br /> <br /> (Placed here for people to check and see if I'm making anything obviously wrong)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> With regards to the Order of Hermes preparations:<br /> <br /> After determining that House Tremere should be destroyed and getting rid of the remaining members of House Tremere among their number in one way or another, they decide to retake the Transylvania tribune. They are aware that Vampires are undead, have supernatural powers, and die in sunlight. They are pretty certain that total destruction or complete separation of the head or heart will destroy a vampire but that even serious injury to the head and heart is probably insufficient. Whether or not they know of the death of the Avatar upon being turned into a vampire they will probably be expecting to fight something akin to awakened Vampires, simply because they have little else to compare what they are facing to. They have a map of Transylvania and will try to take Coeris but are expecting to find other Tremere strongholds throughout the place. They suspect a few areas as Tremere strongholds and plan to storm these places next while minimizing human casualties.<br /> <br /> I'm expecting 4 of the 5 nearby Archmages to take a personal interest in the affair and bring their 2 most combat capable Master students, who will be assisted by their 2 Disciples who will bring their 2 Intitiates. The remaining 6 Houses will probably send a Master each as representative who would likely bring 2 Disciples who would bring 2 students. The Awakened side of the war party would then be 4 Archmagi, 16 Masters, 32 Disciples &amp; 64 Students.<br /> <br /> As the Roman, Greater Alps, Rhine, &amp; Novgorod tribunal have rough control of 6 towns worth of people with a 2500ish people each and could have troops gather in the Greater Alps before heading to Transylvania, they are likely to conscript a 4th of these as troops for 3750 soldiers unless it's more likely that these people will just be in the way. Does anyone have an opinion on this?<br /> <br /> The plan so far is to get up the Alps as quickly as can be, raise a fort of sorts on a mountain a fair distance away from Coeris where they can see Coeris from and keep casting spells (still figuring out their options) from their defensible location until they are fairly sure that resistance has been pummeled and they can sweep the place. Plan B, they turn Coeris into rubble. They will have sunlight 24/7, multiple mages ready to counter any spell they notice the enemy making, and will use magic to prevent the many logistics issues that may come up, including the need for supplies, travel problems, etc. Absolute worst case scenario, they fall back to a secret fort just outside Transylvania in the Alps where they can be reinforced by the rest of the Order.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T21:56:11-07:00","id":1084335,"title":"","content":"That's a lot of other vampires the Tremere had to scrap to make that many gargoyles, not to mention control/dominate into servitude.......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T02:51:45-07:00","id":1084392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084335#post1084335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a lot of other vampires the Tremere had to scrap to make that many gargoyles, not to mention control/dominate into servitude.......</div> </div> </div> </div>After the first batch, you can make them from mortals actually... Also, when you make a gargoyle, they lose the memories of their previous lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-27-2017, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T02:57:38-07:00","id":1084393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084392#post1084392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> After the first batch, you can make them from mortals actually</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean have the gargoyles embrace people? Haha that's funny, The tremere would destroy those that learned or figured out the embrace, it was one of the reasons for the revolt a few centuries later. <br /> <br /> You may lose your memories when you climb out of the vat but that doesn't automatically make you a servant for life, that requires a blood bond and heavy discipline use (both vampiric and traditional) which brings up my next point.<br /> <br /> Since these guys are all out in the middle of nowhere how are that many vampires being supported?<br /> <br /> Granted Transylvania is roughly the size the State of Virginia, you are looking at a fortified structure on a mountain in a region not known for its ease of travel in a time period between large public infrastructure projects a.k.a roads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 04-27-2017, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T03:16:05-07:00","id":1084394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084093#post1084093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also i'd argue that by becoming a clan in 1133 the tremere become part of the &quot;shadowy&quot; vampiric consensus. in other words one could say that attemptin to destroy the tremere clan as a whole is a vulgar act.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Scourge hadn't really developed as a force at this point. Sure, some high-powered rituals (like immortality elixirs) were getting harder and more prone to failure, but it wouldn't be until ~300 years later that you'd see Reality actively fighting back.<br /> <br /> Even if we took the Scourge and moved it centuries earlier, I don't see this as making too much of a difference. Sure, vampires were part of the Consensus of the day (as they are in modern times, because Reasons), but so were wizards. Especially in the Carpathians (where the vampiric overlords were also often kolduns), and <i>especially</i> especially since the Order of Hermes's enemy <i>was also Hermetic</i>. The Tremere's <i>very consors</i> were used to the occult powers wielded by their masters, and therefore would contribute to the local Consensus of what was and was not possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T03:27:00-07:00","id":1084399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084394#post1084394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tremere's very consors were used to the occult powers wielded by their masters, and therefore would contribute to the local Consensus of what was and was not possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, both sides would have their own men at arms (enough to constitute an army is debatable). The Tremere would gain a edge by putting them on the sauce or just wholesale hiring Mercenaries to fortify the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T04:02:07-07:00","id":1084403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084393#post1084393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean have the gargoyles embrace people? Haha that's funny, The tremere would destroy those that learned or figured out the embrace, it was one of the reasons for the revolt a few centuries later.<br /> <br /> Also since these guys are all out in the middle of nowhere how are that many vampires being supported?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, they are supported by the population of Transylvania in my calculations (above). I just assumed, the Tremere would use them in the most pragmatic manner. The Dark ages tremere book seems to note that the Tremere feel they have full control of the Gargoyles and even has mention of testing loyalty by forcing Gargoyle whelps into danger while ordering the Gargoyle who presumably made them to do nothing. There's next to no material about the Revolt in the Dark Ages books I'm reading. I was guessing the reason the revolt happened was because they didn't kill these guys. It only gave them more troops after all, when the gargoyles embraced someone.<br /> <br /> But if the story you know says otherwise, what does it say and how would you suggest I handle them and the numbers they have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-27-2017, 07:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T04:25:02-07:00","id":1084404,"title":"","content":"Again the region is the size of an average American state, how can very large group of vampires stuck in Manhattan feed on the rest of the state of New York? Especially in an age of primitive roads and transportation add a small army laying siege to your castle gray skull and suddenly you can't skip down to the local tavern for a nip of the red stuff. <br /> The number of gargoyles alone would wipe out your stereotypically quaint medieval village in a night.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The revolt happened around the same time as the anarch one, in fact one of the conditions for the Tremere to join the cam was to not only never make gargoyles again but to destroy the ritual and any information regarding it. The Gargoyles section in the lore of the bloodlines gives a lot of information on not only the revolt but the circumstances surrounding their creation in the frist place.<br /> <br /> As per numbers, I would knock them all down by at least 75%. The war quickly became one of attrition and it's really easy to take someone and make them a vampire over hoping through a decade of training they awaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 04-27-2017, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T06:10:37-07:00","id":1084443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084404#post1084404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again the region is the size of an average American state, how can very large group of vampires stuck in Manhattan feed on the rest of the state of New York? Especially in an age of primitive roads and transportation add a small army laying siege to your castle gray skull and suddenly you can't skip down to the local tavern for a nip of the red stuff.<br /> The number of gargoyles alone would wipe out your stereotypically quaint medieval village in a night.</div> </div> </div> </div>5880 Gargoyles can be sustainably fed by a population of 11760 people. That's 5 enslaved towns. This also means that the towns really have to be under the control of the Tremere. Gargoyles can also fly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084404#post1084404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The revolt happened around the same time as the anarch one, in fact one of the conditions for the Tremere to join the cam was to not only never make gargoyles again but to destroy the ritual and any information regarding it. The Gargoyles section in the lore of the bloodlines gives a lot of information on not only the revolt but the circumstances surrounding their creation in the frist place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been going through that but it tells me little of how the Tremere thought of these guys and treated them before the 1200s when they started showing independence. The Tremere Dark ages book says that many Tremere think Gargoyles lack free will, that the magic of the rituals that created them gives them no choice and that the Gargoyles behavior makes them think so. It also clearly states that Gargoyles have free will, of course.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084404#post1084404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As per numbers, I would knock them all down by at least 75%. The war quickly became one of attrition and it's really easy to take someone and make them a vampire over hoping through a decade of training they awaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what can be supported by 1 enslaved town maybe?<br /> Does everyone agree with this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-27-2017, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T08:38:27-07:00","id":1084502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To put you a bit at ease, I am trying to come up with the most exploitative ways to use each side's supernatural capabilities and other resources. For the mages, this currently includes long range catastrophy level effects, sunlight, attacking at day, and possibly dismantling the Tremere stronghold using something like telekinesis or flushing it with a horde of supernaturally enhanced mutated abominations. For the Tremere, it involves the use of the blood bond (which is one of the few things the mages will have little info on at this point), potions, artificially created vampires (gargoyles and their kin) and things like dominating entire populations including little children to try and kill the mages. It's just taking a while and I can't finalize any of it until I figure out what sort of war parties and units each side would build.</div> </div> </div> </div>First I want to thank you for your patience and work. As a fan of the OoH, I can be a bit zealous and I apologize for that. It does put me at ease.<br /> <br /> That being said, I am going to criticize (and give ideas).<br /> <br /> 1.<br /> I don't know enough about the stats of vampires at the time to criticize their charts (albeit I'm surprised there isn't more 6 generation &quot;true Tremere&quot;), but I do have something to say about mage charts:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Archmage (of Forces)<br /> <br /> Willpower 10<br /> Forma 5, Anima 4, Corona 4, <b>Primus 4, Vires 5</b><br /> </div> </div> </div>This thing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . The most powerful mages from the Order, that there is only one per House have 4 in three pillars 5 in one.?<br /> <br /> You know. In DA: Mage corebook there's a cool rote that's called Wrath of Apollo, it's one of the rotes given as exaple for the OoH...and it uses Primus 5 Vires 5.<br /> So, the Order of Hermes can't use their own rotes? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . Nope, I'm not calling with the A word a so called &quot;forces&quot; mage that can't cast the Wrath of Apollo<br /> <br /> In OoH trad book Archmage equals Magister Mundi. In the Grimoire there's a clasification of the ranks of the Order with their minimal Pillar and foundation requirements. A Magister Mundi has to have <i>at least </i>5 in all Pillars and 5 in Forma, but they shouldn't concern you because they are usualy too far gone to care about what transpires in the Order.<br /> The rank just below Archmage, the Master, has a <u>minimun</u> requirement of a Pillar at 5 and Forma 5 (and I don't remember how much in others). I'm not calling Master any mage with less than that. An experienced Master will likely have 2 Pillars at 5, justifying that Golems and the Wrath of Apollo are part of the arsenal suggested for the Order in the books.<br /> <br /> I suggest to change the nomenclatures, leave Archmasters outside of this (they're beings like Tremere himself and the Counsil of Nine) and replace that for Masters (and make a few more, OoH it's likely to have more than one experienced Master per House). Move a point from one Pillar into another to give them enough power to cast cool stuff like Wrath or the Golem creation. Change the Master for Adept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-27-2017, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T09:17:34-07:00","id":1084512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Note that they don't have the same info gathering capabilities as some of the other mage groups of the time nor of the modern version of the Order. For one thing, their use of spirits wasn't quite what it is today. </div> </div> </div>I take note of that, but I think it's worthy to meditate in <i>what they can't and what they can do</i>.<br /> <br /> It's a common mistake (and something that I did for some time) to think that the Pillars of the OoH are Forces, Life, Mind and Prime. They're not. The Pillars are conceptualy more broad than the Spheres, and this amplifies what they can do.<br /> <br /> For Instance: You can summon an Astral Spirit with Corona 4/Primus 2. The very fact that you can do this proves that Corona can fully affect astral spirits (something that Mind alone can't do), as you're basically forcing one to come and then using Primus just to give it a sort of body.<br /> <br /> After forcing a spirit to appear, you can affect them with other spells to doblegate the spirit against their will. Now, a spirit treated this way isn't going to like working for you, but it's going to work for you nevertheless. And if you can summon a fire elemental to attack, so you can summon a more subtle spirit to scout. Consulting spirits should also be possible (except that it's not so much &quot;consulting&quot; as it's torture and interrogation).<br /> Thus, while it's true that &quot; their use of spirits wasn't quite what it is today&quot;, an Adept can still use them to gather info <hr /><br /> Since OoH hasn't a &quot;Correspondence&quot; equivalent: It's impossible for the OoH to affect things outside their &quot;range of view&quot; with magick? .<br /> <br /> I ask this because, while the answer would normaly be yes, DA: Mage has very different rules. You can cast permanent enchantments without anything like &quot;Prime&quot;, and they have a whole section about &quot;casting at range&quot; (I don't remember if it mentions the need of specific Pillars).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-27-2017, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T09:52:25-07:00","id":1084533,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that timing may be a significant factor.<br /> <br /> I mean, the whole reason that the Tremere ended up resorting to vampirism is because they felt their magic becoming less and less effective. Immortality was the big concern, obviously, but the loss of potency and effectiveness seemed to be happening across the board. <br /> <br /> So even though the Hermetic Pillars are amazing, the practitioners are not at the level of strength that they would have been during say 850 AD. They're also about 100 years or so away from the modern Sphere conception of magic. Even if the practical level of deterioration isn't terribly notable (after all, Dark Ages Mage starts around this time), the psychological effects of it might be a factor in why many mages may not be using their magic to full effectiveness, as well as a distraction: since solving the problem of magic is probably considerably higher priority than dealing with a vampire house for a lot of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T10:03:20-07:00","id":1084536,"title":"","content":"One thing: y'know vampires, especially young vampires, don't need to just drink human blood, right? Nothing stopping them from heavily supplementing their diet with animals, especially during war-time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T10:16:35-07:00","id":1084539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084502#post1084502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suggest to change the nomenclatures, leave Archmasters outside of this (they're beings like Tremere himself and the Counsil of Nine) and replace that for Masters (and make a few more, OoH it's likely to have more than one experienced Master per House). Move a point from one Pillar into another to give them enough power to cast cool stuff like Wrath or the Golem creation. Change the Master for Adept.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, just to be clear. Archmaster is gone. The Archmaster Stats I get will likely go to the Masters instead and I should shift them to have 2 Pillars at 5. The Master Stats I have become Adepts, yes?<br /> <br /> Edit: Done in my notes and will use those designations moving forwards. Hopefully people aren't too confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-27-2017, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T10:33:31-07:00","id":1084556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084512#post1084512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I take note of that, but I think it's worthy to meditate in <i>what they can't and what they can do</i>.<br /> <br /> It's a common mistake (and something that I did for some time) to think that the Pillars of the OoH are Forces, Life, Mind and Prime. They're not. The Pillars are conceptualy more broad than the Spheres, and this amplifies what they can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware. Heck, Vires let's you do some stuff that can't be done with just Forces and, weirdly, requires Vires 5 for some Forces 4 effects.<br /> It's altogether a new system.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084512#post1084512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Instance: You can summon an Astral Spirit with Corona 4/Primus 2. The very fact that you can do this proves that Corona can fully affect astral spirits (something that Mind alone can't do), as you're basically forcing one to come and then using Primus just to give it a sort of body.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking the mage would rather do a Corona 4 rote and do their own scouting rather than relying on second hand info.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084512#post1084512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After forcing a spirit to appear, you can affect them with other spells to doblegate the spirit against their will. Now, a spirit treated this way isn't going to like working for you, but it's going to work for you nevertheless. And if you can summon a fire elemental to attack, so you can summon a more subtle spirit to scout. Consulting spirits should also be possible (except that it's not so much &quot;consulting&quot; as it's torture and interrogation).<br /> Thus, while it's true that &quot; their use of spirits wasn't quite what it is today&quot;, an Adept can still use them to gather info <hr /></div> </div> </div> </div>The part of my war plan where they storm Coeris will actually involve a lot of commanding Elementals to do stuff.<br /> <br /> I'm actually aware of real world Hermetic workings and it steers my view of what they would normally do.<br /> All Hermetic practices I've coma across involving spirits simply have the spirits do stuff. There isn't a single one I know for asking info from a spirit. So while it is definitely possible, it never occurred to me as common practice. I'll have them use elemental spy/soldiers once they land.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084512#post1084512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since OoH hasn't a &quot;Correspondence&quot; equivalent: It's impossible for the OoH to affect things outside their &quot;range of view&quot; with magick? .<br /> <br /> I ask this because, while the answer would normaly be yes, DA: Mage has very different rules. You can cast permanent enchantments without anything like &quot;Prime&quot;, and they have a whole section about &quot;casting at range&quot; (I don't remember if it mentions the need of specific Pillars).</div> </div> </div> </div>They can't do it the same way as a Batini or someone with Correspondence. By the rules, they have to be quite close to the target or else difficulty increases dramatically, thus the need to actually be somewhat near Coeris. Otherwise, I'd be having them cast stuff from the safety of their Chantries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-27-2017, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T10:35:25-07:00","id":1084559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084536#post1084536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing: y'know vampires, especially young vampires, don't need to just drink human blood, right? Nothing stopping them from heavily supplementing their diet with animals, especially during war-time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing in particular really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T11:21:51-07:00","id":1084590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084539#post1084539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, just to be clear. Archmaster is gone. The Archmaster Stats I get will likely go to the Masters instead and I should shift them to have 2 Pillars at 5. The Master Stats I have become Adepts, yes?<br /> <br /> Edit: Done in my notes and will use those designations moving forwards. Hopefully people aren't too confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and I hope not. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T11:23:27-07:00","id":1084591,"title":"","content":"Okay. Changing the designations on the Order end shifts some numbers a bit and also has its effects on the Tremere side.<br /> <br /> For the mages, the mages of the 10 remaining founding houses with very roughly 115 per house with very roughly 2 Masters, 4 Adepts, 20 Disciples, &amp; 89 Initiates<br /> In a hundred years, each house would have 4 Master, 8 Adepts, 40 Disciples, &amp; 178 Initiates for a total of 229 per house, and a total of 2290 mages. Each House would probably be supported by people around 4580 people, which would be probably 1 relatively big town (the towns of the era usually having 2500 people but ranging from 1000 to 8000 people).<br /> <br /> For the Vampires, this would give us possibly something like 1 Tremere, 7 Pseudo Elders, 49 Pseudo Ancillae, 343 Pseudo Neonates, &amp; 2401 Fledgelings for a total of 2801 Tremere Vampires. (The Disciples group is gone and the 7 followers of tremere are stronger than I thought). If you want to incorporate some minority of mages, it'll probably be something like 1 Master, 7 Adepts, and 14 Disciples.<br /> <br /> Also, for those who might have missed it,<br /> Shall I lower the Gargoyle numbers from what could comfortably be supported by 5 enslaved towns down to 1 enslaved town?<br /> 5880 to more like 1250?<br /> <br /> Also, for Order Strategy thus far.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking that they would transport themselves to the ideal spot via some sort of Vires 3 Flying carpet rote. That way, each Disciple could handle the transportation of themselves and 2 to 4 others. In a pinch, even an initiate can do the job. Eight of the Adepts could be devoted to making their flying carpets glow with sunlight (Vires 4). They'd be at the corners of the formation, forming something like a cube. Corona 3 could be used to make spies out of flying birds. One or two Adepts would be assigned to this. One or two Adepts will be in charge of bending light to keep the group more or less invisible (Until you enter a certain area and are washed in sunlight). All the Adepts will be in charge of countering spells and Disciples with Primus 3 can also do so in a pinch by lending flying carpet control to one of their initiates. One Master will be in charge of keeping the weather on their side and another (Life Specialist) will probably use Anima 5 to create a number of fantastic creatures you could repeatedly get food from, a bit like those goats from norse mythology you could eat each day and use as beasts of burden afterwards, though these would probably be made happily masochistic using Corona 4. An Master (of Mind) would likely be using Corona 4 to Astrally project around to scout more sensitive areas than an army of birds could manage. Any initiate could use Vires 2 to prevent their group from freezing in the cold and it'll be easy to get water by heating snow using Vires 2.<br /> <br /> This is for getting to the site where they can see Coeris.<br /> <br /> Also, so far, it looks like the order won't bring much of their mundane followers if any to the Alps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-27-2017, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T11:24:03-07:00","id":1084593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084394#post1084394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Scourge hadn't really developed as a force at this point. Sure, some high-powered rituals (like immortality elixirs) were getting harder and more prone to failure, but it wouldn't be until ~300 years later that you'd see Reality actively fighting back.<br /> <br /> Even if we took the Scourge and moved it centuries earlier, I don't see this as making too much of a difference. Sure, vampires were part of the Consensus of the day (as they are in modern times, because Reasons), but so were wizards. Especially in the Carpathians (where the vampiric overlords were also often kolduns), and <i>especially</i> especially since the Order of Hermes's enemy <i>was also Hermetic</i>. The Tremere's <i>very consors</i> were used to the occult powers wielded by their masters, and therefore would contribute to the local Consensus of what was and was not possible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> by that i didn't mean that hermetics would get scourge points by attacking tremere strongholds. it's subtler than that. kind of like the shock reality suffered (partially) because of the death of ravnos and most of his clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T12:52:25-07:00","id":1084644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, so far, it looks like the order won't bring much of their mundane followers if any to the Alps.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I see that transportation of mundane folk by flying carpet could be a problem, I think this diminishes a bit of the lore we have from Ars Magica. If my memory doesn't fail, in Ars each mage has 1 to 3 trusted companions (the guys you will likely give your magic sword if combat capable, or let take care of your finances or other sensitive stuff.) and arround 6 Grogs, servants that do stuff (some act as meat shields).<br /> <br /> Sugestions:<br /> <br /> You could divide the groups between land and sky. Takes more time but makes for a better recognition of the terrain, allows to check nearby chantries. Plus the land group could include the &quot;normal&quot; combat capable folk and would be great to start creating the mythical beasts before arriving.<br /> <br /> Or even better, since you don't care of making a display of power that would alert anyone with the power to detect magick that a storm it's approaching, and since you have powerful Masters of Vires 5, why not go full Hubris and take a cue from Vires 5: the power to <b>make a <i>flying castle</i> </b>. <a href=\"https://1.bp.blogspot.com/_L2gwrkGg4j4/SxDSf9MrCQI/AAAAAAAAAPE/dUFUqz-lymI/s1600/Rosacruces+Casa+Espiritu.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Like this, but flying :P</a> You can keep the flying carpets as a sort of escort/air force and have the mundanes inside. This has the bonus of you don't needing to build a fortress when you arrive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-27-2017, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T13:52:23-07:00","id":1084678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084644#post1084644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or even better, since you don't care of making a display of power that would alert anyone with the power to detect magick that a storm it's approaching, and since you have powerful Masters of Vires 5, why not go full Hubris and take a cue from Vires 5: the power to <b>make a <i>flying castle</i> </b>. <a href=\"https://1.bp.blogspot.com/_L2gwrkGg4j4/SxDSf9MrCQI/AAAAAAAAAPE/dUFUqz-lymI/s1600/Rosacruces+Casa+Espiritu.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Like this, but flying :P</a> You can keep the flying carpets as a sort of escort/air force and have the mundanes inside. This has the bonus of you don't needing to build a fortress when you arrive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much better. And one guy can do it. One guy can make the place glow like the sun. Perfect.<br /> This way, all I decide is wether they each just bring their 1 to 3 trusted servants or the whole army of unnaturally willing and friendly 3750 conscripts.<br /> <br /> Oh, another note, the Stats I built for vampires shifts a bit. The thing I listed as Tremere is now a Pseudo Elder, the Pseudo Elder a Pseudo Ancilla, the Pseudo Ancilla a Pseudo Neonate, the Tremere neonate gone, and the Fledgeling retained. Also, while the Masters got a boost of Vires 4 to 5, the Pseudo Elder got a boost of 2 paths of 3 to 4 (same XP cost. Any comment on the Gargoyle numbers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T14:26:58-07:00","id":1084699,"title":"","content":"Actually, considering castles weren't super big at the time, they'd probably just bring 300 war ready people to supplement their 116 wizards. I shall call it fort S\u00e6hr\u00edmnir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-27-2017, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T00:46:29-07:00","id":1084916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084699#post1084699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, considering castles weren't super big at the time, they'd probably just bring 300 war ready people to supplement their 116 wizards. I shall call it fort S\u00e6hr\u00edmnir.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> and what prevents the tremere from matching them with their own flying castle:?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T10:45:45-07:00","id":1085074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">and what prevents the tremere from matching them with their own flying castle:?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shhh...the Tremere are sliding silently to attack unprotected Chantries (or the least protected they can find). But Hermetics don't know this. Too bad that in DA they can't see the future...<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that this hermetic castle has a lot of power behind it (after all, they're prepared to attack an inexpugnable fortress), and it's invisible. Facing it directly will be much like facing a hammer with a hammer, magick vs magic, I think the strategy the Tremere are using works better for them. However, if you believe that creating a ritual to make flying castles it's a better strategy for the Tremere to counter Hermetics , feel free to argue for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T09:43:46-07:00","id":1086673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1084916#post1084916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> and what prevents the tremere from matching them with their own flying castle:?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I haven't even started on the Tremere side of things. But I'll get there. Sorry it's taking so long. I had a rather eventful vacation this long weekend... the type you need a vacation to recover from. And please post any suggested tactics you might think of from either side of the conflict.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T13:58:28-07:00","id":1086777,"title":"","content":"Once the Hermetics have reached their destination, they attempt to take the castle for themselves.<br /> <br /> One Master of Mind will be scouting around the Tremere base in Astral form, doing what damage can be done by a spellcasting invisible intangible entity.<br /> His or her 2 Adepts will probably be doing the same. This groups remaining 4 disciples will probably be going around improving the morale of the mundane troops and looking for any signs of Tremere meddling with the minds of anyone in the castle. The 8 Initiates of this group will probably be assigned to aid the troops in castle defense.<br /> <br /> One Master will be in charge of flying the castle and keeping it glowing, and maybe the mundane affairs of the castle itself. His 2 Adepts and 4 Disciples will ensure that it remains invisible and that every part of it inside the field of invisibility is awash with sunlight. They\u2019ll probably be in charge of the weather as well. The 8 Initiates of this group will probably be assigned to aid the troops in castle defense.<br /> <br /> One master will be in charge of castle defense, coordinating the 300 soldiers as well as the 2 Adepts &amp; 4 Disciples who can counter magical effects, and the probably any medical needs and mundane stuff like feeding the people and ensuring they have water to drink. The 8 Initiates of this group will probably be assigned to aid the troops in castle defense.<br /> <br /> The remaining Master will be using a Anima 5 &amp; Vires 3 to 5 to create elemental bodies and Corona 4 to force spirits to inhabit these bodies and obey the Master\u2019s commands. This Master\u2019s Adepts, disciples, and initiates will be aiding in this process. There will be Vires 3 air elementals built to steal magic items and spell books and potions and the like; Vires 4 sunlight elementals meant to annihilate vampires and evil wizards in the fortress, and a vires 5 storm elemental meant to destroy any incoming armies and dismantle the enemy castle if that becomes necessary. The body of these could probably be made in one casting by a master &amp; the adepts and disciples with expenditures of willpower and quintessence and a spirit from the astral plane made to inhabit the form in the next hour. (So it takes 2 hours to make 1). I\u2019m supposing they\u2019ll make a bunch of these before leaving (maybe 4 with 8 hours of work) and make the big storm elemental upon landing, The journey itself is about 100 miles and it won\u2019t take them very long to get there by flying castle. Once there, they will keep creating more elemental bodies with spirits in them. At a rate of 1 more every 2 hours.<br /> <br /> All the remaining 6 Adepts and 12 Disciples and 24 Initiates will probably aid in the castle defense with a fair number of them (probably a third of the Adepts and Disciples) capable of countering magic.<br /> <br /> If this fails, the masters will likely just get together to use Vires 5 to blast Coeris into dust, leaving 1 master for defense.<br /> <br /> Since no one else has commented on the Gargoyle numbers, and I don\u2019t entirely agree with what can be sustained by just 1 enslaved town, I will use a number that can be sustained by 2 enslaved normal-sized town or one big town unless someone argues otherwise. This would give us 2500 gargoyles.<br /> <br /> Comments criticisms and suggestions are welcome.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll be figuring out the Vampire side of things next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T07:47:51-07:00","id":1087148,"title":"","content":"Interesting strategies. If Order-wide action is involved, I would just scrounge up and pay some god of fire to turn Ceoris into volcano. With a discount, cuz nobody likes vamps. Of course it would be totally non-epic way to do it, so that's a no.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn the other hand, so it's assumed that Hermetic minions hold back the Trememre ones? Why are the Gargoils included then?<br /> <br /> \u200bIt would actually be interesting how a win in masassa war would affect the order, becoming more organized and martially oriented while retaining their numbers would make a real impact on ascension war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T15:42:14-07:00","id":1087955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1087148#post1087148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Interesting strategies. If Order-wide action is involved, I would just scrounge up and pay some god of fire to turn Ceoris into volcano. With a discount, cuz nobody likes vamps. Of course it would be totally non-epic way to do it, so that's a no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that's roughly what plan B is if they find storming the enemy castle too hard or tedious... actually, they'd probably switch to that if they take any losses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1087148#post1087148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bOn the other hand, so it's assumed that Hermetic minions hold back the Trememre ones? Why are the Gargoils included then?<br /> <br /> \u200bIt would actually be interesting how a win in masassa war would affect the order, becoming more organized and martially oriented while retaining their numbers would make a real impact on ascension war.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I'm still having trouble reading all the vampire power stuff in the Tremere Dark Ages book and the V20 Dark ages book. Work is getting in the way and it is taking longer than I'd like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T03:06:46-07:00","id":1088167,"title":"","content":"To Warpwind,<br /> <br /> Maybe it's not clear. but we haven't run the 1st part of the Massasa war yet. So far, we've only built roughly what the Hermetics are planning to do.<br /> <br /> I'm still making the Vampire side of things and do need help.<br /> <br /> Currently, Coeris is not meant to be the site of any sort of Tremere last stand. The idea was that they'd removed any important documents from the place some time before the start of the war and have transformed it into some sort of death trap in an attempt to cause casualties among the mages. To properly pull this off, they have to offer some resistance to the initial mage attack, then fall to the Hermetic attacking force, all the while fooling the Hermetic spies who will be scouting about in the Astral plane. Their main advantage is that they know a lot of the tricks that Hermetics can do, just not exactly what the Hermetics will do.<br /> <br /> The lack of the Countermagic discipline in V20 Dark Ages is confusing and I'd like to hear more opinions on that.<br /> <br /> Auspex 5 will likely be used for spying on the invading force<br /> Dominate 5 may become useful for possessing the enemy if the opportunity presents itself.<br /> <br /> Other than that, Coeris will be defended by a number of Elementals Summoned using Potestas Elementorum<br /> There will be gargoyles hiding in the castle, ready to pounce upon unsuspecting invaders<br /> They will probably call for fog and a storm to mess with the attacking forces using Potestas Tempestatum <br /> <br /> Defense of the Sacred haven will be used on Coeris so that Sunlight will be rendered harmless<br /> Wake with The Evening's Freshness will be used to prevent the usual dice penalty problems of being attacked in the day<br /> Wards will likely be set against those with Intelligence less than 5 and Strength less than 5 or something like that.<br /> Scry the Hearthstone will probably be important with regards to noticing invisible things in Coeris<br /> Dedicate the haven makes any haven rituals permanent<br /> <br /> I am yet unsure how mortals will play a part in defending Coeris. I'm guessing, the mortal support staff will be Dominated so that every man, woman, and child serving the castle will be a mindless or zealot soldier willing to die for Coeris.<br /> <br /> At least one of the Hermetic Strongholds will be attacked by a large Tremere Force, likely one employing Tremere Vampires specialized in Attack magic, Gargoyles, and Mercenaries or Dominated Conscripts.<br /> <br /> I'm also trying to figure out how best to have a small number of vampiric agents hide amidst the breweries and inns of towns supporting the Hermetic strongholds so they can slowly blood bond the populace and any mages who procure drinksfrom these places. So far, it seems simple in theory with dominate and a few rituals but I have to work this out<br /> <br /> Also, I haven't worked out any of the numbers in any parts of the Tremere end.<br /> <br /> This is what I have so far. Suggestions are welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T00:44:06-07:00","id":1089630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lack of the Countermagic discipline in V20 Dark Ages is confusing and I'd like to hear more opinions on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's confusing? Countermagic was invented for Mage. It's not a thing in games that aren't Mage. Why should it be a thing?. Im pretty sure that if DA had shown more attention in the Massa War it would exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To properly pull this off, they have to offer some resistance to the initial mage attack, then fall to the Hermetic attacking force, all the while fooling the Hermetic spies who will be scouting about in the Astral plane. </div> </div> </div>I'm wondering: how will they do that?. Auspex 2 can detect astral travelers? If so, the plan it's to wait until a disembodied aura appears and talk loudly about fake strategy plans (and pray the disembodied aura doesn't think on reading their minds)?<br /> <br /> I'm surprised Tremere haven't a common ritual against astral intrussion, after all, it's both something they would expect from mages, and something they *do* (two good reasons to have an astral trap in your sanctuary, or something).<br /> <br /> And about Auspex 5, have you decided if vampires &quot;go astral&quot; to the same plane as mages?...because that's something that's never been clarified in the books.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wake with The Evening's Freshness will be used to prevent the usual dice penalty problems of being attacked in the day </div> </div> </div>Correct me if I'm wrong, but isn't that ritual effective only for two turns?. Like, after two turns awakened you're back to having your maximun dice reduced to your Path rating (In V20 it works that way). If that's so, then the (probably ghouled) mortals become more important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dedicate the haven makes any haven rituals permanent </div> </div> </div>Permanent until a Primus 3 disciple or an astral mage dispels them <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T01:51:20-07:00","id":1089649,"title":"","content":"My Guess is the Hermetics didn't really invest deeply into the War. And In my Headcanon Tremere make more use of Mortal Wizards (Sorcerers and to a lesser extent a handful of Mages which are their secret trump cards.).<br /> <br /> My opinion is Those who were mages in Life actually did start off translating a lot of previous magic into Blood Sorcery, but my theory is a lot of the time was being spent coordinating a new Paradigm, aka an Atheist/Mathmatic/Alchemical Blood Sorcery, while a lot of them kept on instinctually making magic that was a lot closer to Hermetic foci and rituals. I see it as a big kickstart that they embraced mages, they started much stronger then normal Neonates, but they just took longer to make their magic Uniform and reliable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T12:27:19-07:00","id":1089889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1089649#post1089649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I see it as a big kickstart that they embraced mages, they started much stronger then normal Neonates, but they just took longer to make their magic Uniform and reliable.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my headcannon any/all Embraced Mages gets abilities appropriate to their Paradigm. This might be easy development of Thaumaturgy or Necromancy, innate and more effective Disciplines knowledge, unique powers (including Disciplines), Merits, and bonuses to Attributes. I also think an Embraced Mage's Avatar survives.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T21:35:22-07:00","id":1093529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1089630#post1089630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's confusing?</div> </div> </div> </div>How it can be used to counter Thaumaturgy and was in the other vampire books and suddenly it's gone in V20 Dark ages.<br /> So, do you think they should have it from the get go? (I'd like other people to pitch in their opinion on this too)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1089630#post1089630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering: how will they do that?. Auspex 2 can detect astral travelers? If so, the plan it's to wait until a disembodied aura appears and talk loudly about fake strategy plans (and pray the disembodied aura doesn't think on reading their minds)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more of an initially strong resistance to attack that gets weaker and eventually breaks into a retreat. Do you think the Tremere would try this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1089630#post1089630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised Tremere haven't a common ritual against astral intrussion, after all, it's both something they would expect from mages, and something they *do* (two good reasons to have an astral trap in your sanctuary, or something).</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, what's your opinion on the interaction of the Tremere Ward ritual and astral travelers. Does it keep them out?<br /> I think it does, but I won't assume my rulings will be what everyone else thinks should be so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1089630#post1089630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And about Auspex 5, have you decided if vampires &quot;go astral&quot; to the same plane as mages?...because that's something that's never been clarified in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll assume they show up on the same plane unless someone has a better idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1089630#post1089630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong, but isn't that ritual effective only for two turns?. Like, after two turns awakened you're back to having your maximun dice reduced to your Path rating (In V20 it works that way). If that's so, then the (probably ghouled) mortals become more important.</div> </div> </div> </div>It says a scene in V20<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1089630#post1089630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Permanent until a Primus 3 disciple or an astral mage dispels them</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough. But it's at least one more mage occupied at that moment.<br /> <br /> Sorry I haven't been around. Seriously, my work is getting in the way.<br /> Does this sound okay, so far?<br /> Any suggestions?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T21:41:01-07:00","id":1093531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1077627-how-could-the-tremere-manage-to-win-the-first-massasa-war?p=1089889#post1089889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my headcannon any/all Embraced Mages gets abilities appropriate to their Paradigm. This might be easy development of Thaumaturgy or Necromancy, innate and more effective Disciplines knowledge, unique powers (including Disciplines), Merits, and bonuses to Attributes. I also think an Embraced Mage's Avatar survives.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to my understanding of the book, they get some measure of magical power (it becomes hell easier to develop appropriate thaumaturgy to the point they get XP for this) but the avatar does die. I'm guessing that thaumaturgy is very much like hermetic hedge magic, but simply using a different power source. Also, someone who knows the secrets of the Corona pillar has a much easier time understanding mental disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T09:01:12-07:00","id":1093677,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, what's your opinion on the interaction of the Tremere Ward ritual and astral travelers. Does it keep them out?<br /> I think it does, but I won't assume my rulings will be what everyone else thinks should be so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess this makes sense, a Ward against Spirits has to work on the other side of the Gauntlet, so it stands to reason that the rest also work that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was thinking more of an initially strong resistance to attack that gets weaker and eventually breaks into a retreat. Do you think the Tremere would try this? </div> </div> </div>I think this makes sense, but in the Astral Plane it would be harder to do...most vampires can't become astral (neither can most mages, but still the numerical advantage of vampires get's reduced. Vampires lose most of their advantages here (no physical attributes, no gargoyles or neonates, no ghouls, you can't carry most of the stuff you need to cast rituals-mages only lose the potential to empower normies and can't bring their disciples).<br /> <br /> As a way to (temporarily) create confusion to the astral travelers, you could leave most of the vampires defending the Chantry believing that they, indeed, have to defend the Chantry to their deaths. Tell them a plan to defend the Chantry that isn't the actual plan. Keep them in the outher perimeter, and Ward inner regions of the Chantries. That way, mages would discover the &quot;true plans to protect the chantries&quot; from the minds of genuine Tremere vampires, and would think that the Warded areas are important, but won't know why (they are important because here's where most of the traps will be laid, and where the few Elders that know the plan are hidding to enact any ritual that needs to be enacted, pull any lever than needs to be pulled, and then try to flee). Warding the entire chantry isn't a bad idea either, not because it will work, but because it would be a credible effort, and the least Hermetics know the better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How it can be used to counter Thaumaturgy and was in the other vampire books and suddenly it's gone in V20 Dark ages.<br /> So, do you think they should have it from the get go? </div> </div> </div>While it may not be in V20DA, I think it was present in DA,(in the book of the Low Clans?). I think they should have it.]<br /> <br /> As for suggestions:<br /> <br /> Hermetics have the best Pillar to detect and counter any form of supernatural power. Don't neglect sensory magic and unweaving. Attacking a mage stronghold should prioritize these two from the get go (and, quite frankly, it would be a shame to have all those Sun Elementals unable to work just because the enemy casted magical darkness <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).<br /> Knowing this, Tremere could built mundane, mechanical, traps to argument the defense. While these could potentially be detected by any human, they won't be shining like fireworks (well, mages could try something with Vires to sense mundane traps as weirdness in the forces present in the architecture, but most Hermetics lack good masonry skills to understand the data...hears Craftmason laughing far away).<br /> <br /> Also, while Hermetics don't want to damage the chantry, start the main wave of the attack with a bang could be appropiate. Blowing up the outer walls shouldn't damage important books and artifacts, and would create big holes from where the beasts and elementals can enter easily (and to retreat, if it were necessary). It's also a way to see how well warded it's the fortress, to dismantle mundane weapons laying near the walls, to destroy guard rooms that are usually near to the outer perimeter, and to provoke a reaction. You can always rebuild them again if you want to stay (with Vires and earth elementals, it shouldn't take too long)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm also trying to figure out how best to have a small number of vampiric agents hide amidst the breweries and inns of towns supporting the Hermetic strongholds so they can slowly blood bond the populace and any mages who procure drinksfrom these places. So far, it seems simple in theory with dominate and a few rituals but I have to work this out </div> </div> </div>In order to figure this you need to think on how it's the relationship of mages and these places, and how this changes with war. Hermetic Chantries are supposed to be in isolated places, so the mages probably don't go a lot to the town (young mages do, of course, to have fun), since chantries are supposed to harbor a small population of mortals alongside mages, it's likely that they send people to get drinks and food to supply (a big chantry may be like a small town unto itself).<br /> If they're waiting an attack from vampires, it's likely they will sleep at day, and go out at night. Going to the town it's to be discouraged because it would risk being attacked by surprise (nor that mages will always comply) .<br /> <br /> It's also likely mages will be searching for magic in the surrounding areas, because being in war with a House it's to expect a magical attack. This has some implications. Like sneaking drinks with vitae to the Chantry might not be possible (evil death magick it's not something you want to find in your drink, and guards are going to be searching for magic).<br /> The Chantries may have animals, people, and perhaps even a spirit or two, looking for big movements of &quot;people&quot; in the night. And for magic. So laying low may be the best strategy.<br /> <br /> A lot of Rituals protecting areas may be detected, so it's a risk to employ them in big numbers before you're ready to make the attack.<br /> <br /> It's...debatable...if Blood Bonding an entire village should attract attention of someone searching for Tremere movements in the surrounding area. It's magic so it can be detected, but it may be subtle enough to not be (you don't need to have Vitae in your system to remain bonded, but it's still a form of strong mind-control of mystical nature).<br /> Personaly, I think that it should be possible to sense these kind of stuff , but Hermetics (not knowing the blood bond and not caring for mortals) aren't going to carefully search the villages, focusing instead on keeping tabs on the roads, and on big acts of magic. Eventually, the ressonance of an entire bonded population may be too much to not be detected casually, but when the village reaches that point it would be already too late (and, I guess, the Tremere would launch their attack)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}